From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:51:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libprocessgroup: treat a missing cgroup hierarchy as a no-op,
 not an error

Second boot attempt got 4x further (14.5s vs 3.5s) but still ended in
'bootstrap-apexd-failed'. With the cgroup v2 root removed from cgroups.json,
the CGROUPV2_CONTROLLER_NAME lookups leave the hierarchy path empty, and
createProcessGroupInternal then tries to create '/uid_0' on the read-only
rootfs:

  libprocessgroup: Failed to make and chown /uid_0: Read-only file system
  init: Command 'start ueventd' ... failed: Could not start service:
        createProcessGroup...
  init: Service 'apexd-bootstrap' failed to start due to a fatal error

The earlier read of these call sites was half right: they do not crash on an
absent v2 root, but returning an error from createProcessGroup IS fatal to
service startup, so 'degrades safely' was wrong.

There is nothing to create when no hierarchy is configured, so return success
instead. KillProcessGroup already copes -- the same boot logged 'Successfully
killed process cgroup uid 0'.
---
 libprocessgroup/processgroup.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libprocessgroup/processgroup.cpp b/libprocessgroup/processgroup.cpp
index 267e62c67..fe6aa8d59 100644
--- a/libprocessgroup/processgroup.cpp
+++ b/libprocessgroup/processgroup.cpp
@@ -494,6 +494,19 @@ int killProcessGroupOnce(uid_t uid, int initialPid, int signal, int* max_process
 
 static int createProcessGroupInternal(uid_t uid, int initialPid, std::string cgroup,
                                       bool activate_controllers) {
+    // ether/msm8992: no cgroup v2 hierarchy exists on this kernel (cgroup v2 landed in Linux 4.5;
+    // this is 3.10), so cgroups.json declares no Cgroups2 root and the CGROUPV2_CONTROLLER_NAME
+    // lookups in our callers leave `cgroup` empty. Without this guard ConvertUidToPath("") yields
+    // "/uid_0", MkdirAndChown then fails on the read-only rootfs, and the non-zero return is fatal
+    // to starting a service:
+    //   libprocessgroup: Failed to make and chown /uid_0: Read-only file system
+    //   init: Command 'start ueventd' ... failed: Could not start service: createProcessGroup...
+    // which takes down ueventd and apexd-bootstrap and reboots the device. There is nothing to
+    // create when there is no hierarchy, so report success and let the caller proceed.
+    if (cgroup.empty()) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     auto uid_path = ConvertUidToPath(cgroup.c_str(), uid);
 
     struct stat cgroup_stat;
